Another journal that I kept of my latest ascension; enjoy!

Halfar the Female Human Knight, 12/15/06

6:00 PM
"You ascend to the status of demi-god..."
My eleventh character goes to join the ranks of adventurers assembled
at the demi-god cafe.
No less than ten consecutive attempts failed before I finally ascended
the Healer.
My addiction for today is cured, no?

6:30 PM
No. I browse the list of roles, and choose the next one on the list.
A Knight. I have yet to ascend one. Give it another shot?
Welcome to the dungeon, Halfar the female human Knight.
My familiar abode, hangout, sanctuary.
I mount Peanuts the pony. I do not slip.
Things are looking up already.

6:45 PM
An altar on dungeon level two. It's chaotic, but it will serve my
purposes.
I identify the few scrolls that I picked up, then move on.
A fairly large armour shop, on the other end of the level?
I enter warily, as does Peanuts. I noticed that I have some treats for
my new best friend.
Decked out in my new attire, and with a decent amount of gold from
resale, I move on.
A scroll shop on the next level? Just my luck.
I rob the shopkeeper and avoid the mimic.

7:15 PM
The mines await. I venture down, to a darkened level.
My long sword passes easily through the gnomes.
As do I, through a trapdoor.
Another darkened level. It is where my many other incarnations have met
their demise.
And indeed, I have died once before here. Halfar the Healer's ghost
arrests me.
I find his bonespile, with a three-by-three pile of boulders nearby. A
recent death.

7:30 PM
The two-thousand-odd zorkmids of Halfar's I take with me.
His stethoscope, his wand, and what are bound to be his healing potions
I stash too.
I find the stairs down, and to my relief I arrive in a lit room.
A full identify had confirmed that I have three scrolls of enchant
weapon, and my sword is now +3.
The few gnomes that bar my way are cut down, and I enter the temple.
Lugh's priest awaits.
I quickly sacrifice a few more loiterers to the Lawful Celt.
"Use my gift wisely!" I see here a longsword named Sunsword.
And I'd just bought a brass lantern, too.

7:45 PM
The rest of the mines is no match for Sunsword.
A second identify reveals that the gray stone in my inventory is a
luckstone.
I browse Mine's End briefly, learn 'fireball' at 100% fail, and return
to make holy water.
Terry, of my previous game, had made good use of 'fireball' and 'cone
of cold'.
I do not make the greatest of healers.

8:00 PM
I find Peanuts on my return trip, and I calm him down with another
apple. We ride up to the light.
I go down the main dungeon branch. I open a chest, and engrave-id the
first wand of the game.
"For what do you wish?"
I panic. This had just happened to me a short month ago.
But you can never really get used to the surprise. I quickly get a +2
silver dragon scale mail.
Picking it up and putting it on it, a Woodland-elf ambushes me. If it
wasn't for that armor shop, I'd be dead.
AC -14. I slay the elf and his posse. Returning to the wand of wishing,
I recall - I am uncertain of the charges.
I use up my last scroll of identify, and target the wand. It is (0:1).
I know what to wish for now.

8:15 PM
The wand is at (1:3). My dilemma reasserts itself.
If I was playing a neutral spellcaster, I would have no problem. But as
a lawful hack-and-slash?
Magic resistance is key. But I have armor and a weapon already. Is
there nothing that I need?
Perhaps I could go for a figurine of an Archon, but it is risky. If it
comes out hostile, it's game over.
Now that I think about it, perhaps gray dragon scale mail and a shield
of reflection would have been a better combination.

8:30 PM
I decide to continue, undecided.
A scroll of identify on the floor gives me my third full identify of
the game. I am scared.
The RNG never forgets; the RNG never forgives.
That horn? A frost horn (0:7). That ring? A +4 ring of protection.
It reminds me of the time I found a randomly generated +5 helm of
brilliance.
I must play NetHack too much.

8:45 PM
I am ambushed by a water moccasin. Another bones level.
Again, it is Halfar the Healer, another failed attempt. I scavenge his
items and produce more holy water.
My next destination is Sokoban.
I arrive, skirting the edge of a leprechaun hall, and stashing parts of
my cumbersome inventory into scattered chests.
Peanuts is slain while I am atop him, and I suddenly find myself riding
a statue.
I cut down the rest of the chickatrices, and note to return for the
steed's saddle.

9:00 PM
It is the amulet of reflection ending. I don't bother with it; the last
of my characters to enter that level never left it.
A wish goes towards a bag of holding. I continue exploring, and find an
altar two levels below.
I do not manage to convert it with a plains centaur, and I continue.
The wraith corpse that I eat rots away completely.
Perhaps my luck is changing for the worse?

9:15 PM
A levelporter returns me to dungeon level 2. I take the opportunity to
make a few sacrifices and pray for holy water.
Quaffing my potions, I break out in hives. Nothing that a unicorn horn
won't heal, though.
I return to the Oracle level and dilute more potions. All of the
fountains there dry up.

9:30 PM
Lugh has a temple set up in dungeon level 11. I have just enough to buy
one more point of protection.
I return to the Quest level, and stumble into the portal. King Arthur
rejects my services.
Brigit has a temple in dungeon level 17. I continue on.
A gray unicorn is hit by a rock when retreating. I eat its corpse.
While digging a passage, an air elemental engulfs and almost kills me.
I should use up my last three wishes.

10:00 PM
An elf has read a scroll of earth in a narrow passage. Neither of our
leather helms protected us.
I backtrack for a few levels, then return with a pick-axe and a
vengance.
A few dreary pre-castle levels; Medusa's titan is peaceful. I dig down.
The castle emerges before me. I take up the spot adjacent to the
drawbridge, then attempt to burn Elbereth.
My lack of a wand of fire or lightning deters me; yet I continue to
lower the drawbridge.
The potion of object detection I saved is used; the chest is located.
A tooled horn is my new best friend; many fall before the might of the
drawbridge.

10:15 PM
I enter the courtyard, and survey my surroundings. A disenchanter
approaches.
The crowd of monsters grows thick. I am bogged down; no choice but to
retreat. I crush the minotaur on my way out.
That mirror I saved finally comes into use; Medusa may be the prettier
but at least I am still alive.
Time to return to the castle. A pair of liches and a few giants await.
They all sample Sunsword.
I must have forgotten to close the drawbridge in my hasty retreat. A
battallion of soldiers confronts me.
None of the welcoming party survive; I dash into the castle. More
troops defend the wand; I parry and thrust.
Managed to squeeze through the crowd and the hallway. I take sanctuary
in the wand room.
Success.

Halfar the Female Human Knight, 12/16/06
5:30 PM
Another day of life, another night of playing NetHack.
I wish for a blessed greased fixed magic marker. I get +0.
I write up two scrolls of charging, and zap the Castle's wand.
For what do I wish? A blessed fixed greased +3 helm of brilliance.
I get +0. I enchant it twice and get +4. Fair enough for a catiff.
The storerooms are soon cleared, and I retrieve an elven dagger named
Sting.
Time to descend to the Valley.

6:00 PM
The blessed rustproof +7 Sunsword makes short work of the undead.
I pick up a long sword and begin to two-weapon. Why didn't I remember
to do this with my original long sword?
Though I am wearing elven boots, I walk into the squeaky board before
the temple of Moloch.
Fending off the hordes of undead, I am level-drained twice, but manage
to regain the level each time.
Soon I eat two wraith corpses, and am now at XP:15. Ixoth, beware!
I learn detect monsters, and cast it until my mana is gone. Then I
realize that Knights cannot advance divination.
Time to return to the castle.

6:30 PM
I turn a potion to water, and dilute the next one before the fountain
dries up.
Nothing to see here, time to move along.
An electric eel grabs me on Medusa's level, and breaks apart half a
dozen of my wands.
Fortunately, I've stashed my wands of wishing, which are at (1:1) and
(1:3), respectively.
Six more wishes and nothing to wish for. I suspect that I'll wish for
teleport control soon.
On the level above, I identify a ring that I had picked up from the
Valley. Teleport control.
It is a swamp level. I clear a room and set up a skinny-dipping pool.
The single entryway is now blocked with a boulder, with Elbereth burnt
beneath it.
I dilute and blank my undesired potions and scrolls. Did my charisma
increase after the bath?

7:00 PM
Time to take up the Quest. I descend and find the Isle of Glass.
I use the neutral altar and merge my potions of water.
An ochre jelly dissolves a spider web. I am surprised.
The nemesis level looms ahead. A few quasits fall into pits, and I make
myself a tin of tengu meat.
Ixoth appears, and casts a few spells. I zap him with a wand of sleep.
He dozes, and I am rebuked for hitting a sleeping monster.
I retrieve the Bell, the Mirror, and a tin of Ixoth meat.

7:30 PM
I go up a few more levels. It is past 16000 turns, and I still have 6
wishes left.
Why didn't I use them? Might as well now. I conjure up a blessed fixed
greased spellbook of magic missile.
Teleporting back to the Valley of the Dead, I wrest the last charge
from my original wand of wishing.
The speed boots came +0. Attacking fleeing monsters must have lowered
my luck.
I delve into Gehennom.

8:00 PM
A minotaur drops a cursed -1 katana, which I use in place of my
corroded +0 long sword.
I enchant it up to +6, after failing two attempts to get it to +7.
Some hill giants appear, and one of them leaves a wand that stops bugs.
I identified wands of sleep yesterday.
Baalzebub whispers into thin air, and gets angry! Looks like I'll have
to kill him.
I stumble into a sleeping gas trap, and fall asleep. Baalzebub has no
mercy...
I survive until he summons Dispater. While asleep, Dispater asks for
money for safe passage.
A bug! How much will I offer? I give the demon 3 zorkmids while
snoozing, and he vanishes.
My tinning kit comes to great use, and I gain sleep resistance, shock
resistance, and some strength.
I locate the Wizard at dungeon level 42. This is a deep hell.

8:15 PM
I wish for another magic marker. With this I can write scrolls of magic
mapping.
Besides, I could consider using the silver sabre that I just picked up
if it is enchanted.
I enter a fake tower entrance, and fight my way out of the hordes that
a demi-lich has summoned.
Then I notice that I had gone the last 1000 turns without my speed
boots on.
I continue, now switching to the silver sabre, which I have enchanted
to +7.
Three more purple Ls fall before my cockatrice corpse, yet none leave
an athame.
I trigger a land mine.
After further exploration, the real entrance presents itself, and I
enter.
The red dragon gets tinned, and eaten, to complete my mandatory
resistance collection.

8:30 PM
It is turn number 19448, and I tag the vibrating square with an iron
chain, after searching through half the level.
A cockatrice left a corpse; it is time to pay Orcus a visit.
The corpse rots away while I am searching for the stairs up, five or
six levels above.
A boulder triggers a pit! How does one exactly trigger a pit?
Turn 20000, and I am stuck on level 41, not knowing where the up-stairs
are.
On level 39, I finally decide to use my last blank scroll for magic
mapping. I find two up-stairs.

8:45 PM
I retrieve the amulet of lifesaving and water walking boots.
To Vlad I show no kindness; I move straight into him with the blessed
+7 Sunsword and a blessed +7 silver sabre.
A white unicorn is spawned, and I toss it five gems to bring my luck
back up.
I find that I only have five candles to attach to the Candelabrum;
perhaps I'll need to use a wish.

9:00 PM
I whack Orcus with my rubber chicken, and is petrified by my offense.
In the town, I find Mjollnir, as well as three candles.
The candles get attached, and the hammer is ditched, stuck firmly
beneath a boulder.
With the potions of full healing I've picked up, I increase my maximum
health to 150.
What a scrawny knight! That's with all of the potions blessed, too!
I accidentally break my wand of death, when trying to use my tinning
kit.
There is no excuse for this.

9:30 PM
I am satisfied that I have mapped all of the levels of Gehennom, and
I'm off to see the Wizard.
The lich that guarded the first ladder up was standing on top of an
amulet of lifesaving.
An incubus flirts with me and is disintegrated in the same turn. I
should kill that mind flayer first.
I find a spellbook of identify after the zoo. Without wearing metal, I
have a 69 percent fail.
The priests of Moloch will have robes.

9:45 PM
With my remaining wand of death, I shoot the Wizard of Yendor.
The first ray hits him.
I eat his dog and tin his corpse, then take his artefact for my own
devious devices.
Time to leave the tower.

10:00 PM
I see that I have 2 cursed scrolls of teleportation. Might as well use
them.
Levelport back to dungeon level 11, and donate to the priest of Lugh.
I don't have anything to sacrifice, so I use the second scroll to go to
dungeon level 55.
"The odor of stench and decay pervades through the air."
Alas. I quest through the levels of hell again, and pick up a
cockatrice corpse.
Rodney manifests himself, and I bash him until he goes away. I
continue.
It is only until my cockatrice corpse rots away that I realize that I
could have made a statue of him.
Oh well; at least he won't bother me in the Sanctum.

10:15 PM
I enter the Sanctum. The need for conflict presents itself; I use up a
wish.
A priest reads a scroll of earth and blocks the entrance to the left
half of the level.
My wand of striking is out of charges; I resort to teleporting it.
I quaff a brown potion and merge with my silver dragon scale mail.
After carefully avoiding and using daggers to kill a cockatrice, the
game tells me that I'm living a healthy lifestyle.
I manage to get slain by a captain, and return to my human form.
The high priest stands in my beam of fire, and he goes down.
The Amulet of Yendor named the Real Deal rests in my inventory, and I
make my way back.
A magic trap parked in front of a door unleashes four bone devils and
four Gray-elves.
I'm more concerned about the disenchanter in front of me.
The blue R becomes a white @, and the wayfarer flees. I too flee, and
exit the Sanctum.

10:30 PM
A pit fiend somehow drowns in the Sanctum's moat. I try not to do the
same.
The mysterious force pesters me, and I use up the rest of my scrolls of
teleportation.
Asemodeus had not been slain, so it turns out, and Rodney made his
appearance again.
Time to wish for another wand of death, so it seems.
There was an uncursed scroll of charging that I pull out, bless, and
recharge my wand of death with.
Finally, I exit Gehennom. I have only a few charges left in my last
wand of teleportation.
But I do come across a leprechaun hall that I had passed by earlier; I
will try to get teleportitis.
I finally manage to get it after killing almost a dozen leprechauns.
Time to head on out.
"The leprechaun hits the leprechaun! The leprechaun steals some gold
from the leprechaun."

10:45 PM
That potion shop that I didn't bother to buy from? Perfect target for
robbing.
It has two potions of full healing, and one of healing. Nothing more
impressive than that, I'm afraid.
"You drop the Amulet of Yendor named the Real Deal. Elm seems
uninterested."
I escape the shop without paying, and the Keystone Kops come after me.
I seem uninterested, and continue up the dungeon.

11:00 PM
It is turn 26516. I wrest the last charge from the worn-out castle
wand, for a wand of death. This is it.
I escape the dungeon without paying, and the Wizard of Yendor comes
after me.
He, along with the Elvenking, bites my death ray, and I detect the
portal.
I drop my one last wand of digging. In my last ascension yesterday, I
dropped 7 such wands.
The only spell that has expired is fireball, and I confuse myself. I
put on my ring of levitation, and jump in the portal.
The Plane of Air went very smoothly. I detected the portal, due right
of me, and headed straight towards it.
Only one air elemental engulfed me, courtesy of my ring of conflict,
before I made it to the Plane of Fire.
The portal was in the centre of the map, and I made it easily.
The Plane of Water was far better than yesterday; I detected the portal
and found it after only a few stray moves.

11:15 PM
"You have been worthy of me!"
And indeed, my Knight has been worthy. Famine guards the left, Death
the centre. I go left.
Conflict brings a few angels around me; all the better for killing the
obligatory purple Ls.
But no purple Ls show up this time. By the time I enter the left
chamber, Famine is already dead.
Something killed it in less than ten moves; hopefully I don't suffer
the same fate.
I do not jump towards the altar; instead I use the last two charges of
my wand of teleportation to clear the door.
Janet the invisible Ryoshu cleaves her way towards me as I cut down
dragons to move in her direction.
>From behind, Maud the invisible Pioneer tries to pin me in. It sounds
like the plotline for a women's wrestling match.
As Janet fells a priest of Manannan Mac Lir, I open the door to the
temple.
Wands are fired in my direction but inevitably bounce off; the dual
joys of reflection and magic resistance.
The altar is Lugh's. I offer the Amulet, and am bathed in radiance; I
have completed my fourth ascension of this week.



